PHOTO-011 phase 2 (adjustment layers) is implemented on branch
feat/PHOTO-011-adjustment-layers — check `gh pr list` before assuming it's
merged. PHOTO-011 stays unticked: the local adjustment brush and
graduated/radial filters are still to come.

What phase 2 added, and what's worth knowing before phase 3:
- Store: ToneAdjustments is now its own type (every tone/colour/levels/
  curves/detail field). PhotoAdjustments extends it with geometry, the base
  selection, and `layers: AdjustmentLayer[]` (id, name, visible, opacity,
  selection = its mask, adjustments: ToneAdjustments).
- The *active target* (activeLayerId, UI state, not history) decides what
  the panels and selection tools edit. Every tone setter goes through
  commitTone, every selection action through commitSelection; the panels read
  selectActiveTone / selectActiveSelection. A dangling id falls back to base.
- addLayer moves the base selection (if any) into the new layer's mask, so
  "select, add layer, adjust" is the flow. No mask = whole photo.
- renderAdjustedImage: fast path unchanged when there's no base selection
  and no visible non-neutral layer. Otherwise it works from the framed
  original's pixels: base tone inside the base selection, then each layer on
  the result so far, inside its mask and at its opacity (applyTone). Masks
  are cached per selection object and render size.
- Scratch canvases for the CSS-filter step are reused only up to 2.5 MP; a
  full-size bake uses one-off canvases (memory).

Suggested phase 3: the local adjustment brush and graduated/radial filters
as *new mask kinds* on the same layers — extend PhotoSelection's op list with
'stroke' (brush dabs: points + radius + hardness, add/erase) and 'gradient'
(linear: two points; radial: centre + radii + feather) ops, rasterized in
renderSelectionMask like polygons. No new layer model needed.

PHOTO-014 (cut/copy/paste a selection as a movable layer) builds on this
layer stack — but these are *adjustment* layers; a pixel layer is new.

